  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.593,
      "end": 3.8,
      "text": "One of the world's biggest travel platforms once had to sell cereal"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.88,
      "end": 5.519,
      "text": "just to keep its startup alive."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.861,
      "end": 9.775,
      "text": "Back in 2007, Brian Chesky and Joe Gebbia had a problem:"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.06,
      "end": 11.677,
      "text": "they couldn't easily afford their rent."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.9,
      "end": 13.626,
      "text": "During a busy design conference,"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.781,
      "end": 16.691,
      "text": "they turned their apartment into a tiny accommodation business,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.869,
      "end": 18.645,
      "text": "using air mattresses for guests."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.973,
      "end": 22.499,
      "text": "But turning that idea into a business was harder than they imagined."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.664,
      "end": 24.92,
      "text": "Bookings were limited, money was running out,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.064,
      "end": 27.616,
      "text": "and the founders were struggling to keep the company going."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.949,
      "end": 30.622,
      "text": "Then, during the 2008 US election,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.928,
      "end": 34.631,
      "text": "they created something unusual: Obama O's and Cap'n McCain's."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.848,
      "end": 36.904,
      "text": "They designed collectible cereal boxes,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.188,
      "end": 40.476,
      "text": "assembled them by hand, and sold them for forty dollars each."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.794,
      "end": 44.216,
      "text": "The unusual experiment brought in around thirty thousand dollars."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.436,
      "end": 46.125,
      "text": "It wasn't a scalable business model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.291,
      "end": 48.932,
      "text": "but it gave Airbnb money to keep going and a story"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.012,
      "end": 51.519,
      "text": "that would eventually attract the attention of investors."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.849,
      "end": 54.623,
      "text": "That persistence helped them get into Y Combinator."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.888,
      "end": 57.071,
      "text": "But they still had to solve the real problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.288,
      "end": 58.565,
      "text": "They travelled to New York,"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.728,
      "end": 62.103,
      "text": "met hosts, and personally improved their property photographs."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.328,
      "end": 65.564,
      "text": "They focused on making the marketplace better for real people."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.905,
      "end": 68.528,
      "text": "Airbnb became a global travel platform."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.764,
      "end": 72.301,
      "text": "But the early lesson was already clear: when the obvious solution fails,"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.544,
      "end": 77.05,
      "text": "creativity, persistence, and understanding your customers can open another door."
    }
  ]
}
